This document provides guidelines for emergency management of cascading event. It includes:
- Characteristics of cascading event in the perspective of emergency management;
- Principles of emergency management of cascading event;
- Guidelines for cascading event identification;
- Guidelines for establishing foundation of cascading event management;
- Guidelines for prevention, preparedness and response of cascading event in emergency management process.
This document is applicable to any level organizations, urban resilience authorities with responsibility and accountability for, or involvement in, part of all emergency management process of cascading event.

This document provides guidelines for organizations working with communities to develop, establish and support community emergency hubs that contribute to societal resilience to disruption. 

This document includes:

—	a framework of the aim, objectives and principles for community emergency hubs;
—	guidance on engaging communities in the development of community emergency hubs;
—	guidance on organizing, equipping and aligning community emergency hubs with community plans;
—	guidance on preparing volunteers to work to work safely, collaboratively and with appropriate leadership; 
—	guidance on identifying community needs, coordinating offers of support, and providing other community support services; 
—	guidance on activating, operating and closing community emergency hubs;
—	guidance on supporting community recovery following disruption.
